{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '235,340p' network.js; sed -n '145,210p' scene.js; rg -n 'harness|test|duration|dedicated' hub/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"    return sent;\n  }\n  sendInput(input) {\n    this._input = cleanInput(input);\n    if (this._input.pop) this._popQueued = true;\n  }\n  update(dt, state) {\n    if (!this.connected || !this.canPlay) return;\n    this._sendClock += Math.min(Math.max(0, dt || 0), 0.25);\n    const interval = this.role === 'host' ? 0.1 : 1 / 15;\n    if (this._sendClock < interval) return;\n    this._sendClock %= interval;\n    if (this.role === 'guest') {\n      const input = { ...this._input, pop: this._input.pop || this._popQueued };\n      if (this._send({ t: 'input', input }, this.hubActive ? this._hub.host : undefined)) this._popQueued = false;\n    }\n    else if (state != null) {\n      this._lastScore = Number.isFinite(state.score) ? state.score : this._lastScore;\n      const packet = { t: 'state', seq: this._sequence++, state };\n      // Client protocol limits each JSON message to 16 KiB.\n      if (this.hubActive && JSON.stringify(packet).length > 16000) {\n        this.metrics.rejected++;\n        if (this.metrics.rejected === 1) this._status('World snapshot exceeds the AI Hub message limit.');\n        return;\n      }\n      this._send(packet);\n    }\n  }\n  finish(won, score = this._lastScore, stats) {\n    if (this.role !== 'host' || this.ended || this._reported) return false;\n    this._reported = true;\n    const value = Number.isFinite(score) ? score : 0;\n    if (this.hubActive) {\n      const ids = this.players.map((p) => p.id);\n      this._hub.finish({ standings: [ids], scores: Object.fromEntries(ids.map((id) => [id, value])), won: won === true,\n        ...(stats ? { stats: Object.fromEntries(ids.map((id) => [id, stats])) } : {}) });\n    } else this._send({ t: 'finish', won: won === true, score: value });\n    return true;\n  }\n  disconnect(notify = true) {\n    // AI Hub owns session lifetime; game menus cannot leave, restart or quit it.\n    if (this.hubActive) return false;\n    this._generation++;\n    const connection = this._connection;\n    this._connection = null;\n    connection?.close();\n    this._peer?.destroy();\n    this._peer = null;\n    this.role = 'offline'; this.connected = false; this.started = false; this.ended = false;\n    this.roomCode = ''; this.me = 0; this.server = false;\n    this._sendClock = 0; this._sequence = 0; this._receivedSequence = -1;\n    this._reported = false; this._startAt = Infinity; this._popQueued = false;\n    this._input = { x: 0, pop: false };\n    this._roster([]);\n    if (notify) this._status('Play together. Catch together.');\n    return true;\n  }\n  inspect() {\n    return { role: this.role, connected: this.connected, roomCode: this.roomCode, players: this.players,\n      me: this.me, server: this.server, hubActive: this.hubActive, started: this.started,\n      ended: this.ended, canPlay: this.canPlay, status: this.status, metrics: { ...this.metrics } };\n  }\n}\n11:The hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\n12:described in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n15:- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n21:> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n194:  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n316:## Test it\n318:The harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\n323:curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n329:Then open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\n330:The hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n352:game is served from the harness's own origin.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '316,360p' hub/README.md; rg -n 'resize|inspect' scene.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '316,360p' hub/README.md; rg -n 'resize|inspect' scene.js\"","aggregated_output":"## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n21:  this.buildStage();this.buildBomber();this.buildPlayers();this.resize();\n137: resize(){if(!this.renderer)return;const w=this.container.clientWidth||innerWidth,h=this.container.clientHeight||innerHeight;this.renderer.setSize(w,h);const aspect=w/h;const halfH=Math.max(8.15,11.8/ [... omitted end of long line]\n140: inspect(){return {ready:this.ready,backend:this.renderer?.backend?.isWebGPUBackend?'webgpu':'webgl',renders:this.renderCount,bombs:this.bombMeshes.size,particles:this.particles.length,animationClips: [... omitted end of long line]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
