{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'lastDevice =|splash.*ready|scrollTop|ABOUT THE SHOW' main.js; rg -n 'charge.*style' main.js; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='credits.json';s=json.load(open(p));s['testingFeedback']=['Testing caught 8 issues: offline audio initialization, two visual defects, invalid mouse coordinates, online seat IDs, missing Hub tags, a Rapier sensor crash and split-bomb AI targeting. All were fixed.','4 critical issues: invalid mouse coordinates, unusable online seat mapping, missing required Hub metadata and the Rapier runtime crash.','The scripted five-round playthrough: it exposed the physics crash and split-bomb targeting problem, then verified every mechanic through victory.','Headless WebGPU screenshots were least useful because this host can return a blank canvas. Runtime checks verified WebGPU; WebGL captures verified composition.'];s['engineFeedback'][1]='I initially passed a pointer-coordinate object as a number and assumed bucket sensors would be harmless. Integration tests corrected the input contract; repeated physics cleanup exposed a sensor failure, so catching uses a swept crossing test while Rapier drives the bombs.';s['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Chromium: complete five-round playthrough, keyboard / mouse / emulated standard gamepad / touch, offline audio waveform checks, real two-page WebRTC rooms, and all four AI Hub harness scenarios; 1920×1080 and portrait visual captures. Physical controllers, real phones, audible listening and external NAT traversal: unknown.';open(p,'w').write(json.dumps(s,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
